### 9. Data Limitations and Assumptions

- The accuracy of dashboard results depends on the quality and completeness of the source datasets.
- Missing values may affect certain calculations and visualisations.
- Account and card status values must be interpreted consistently.
- Delayed payment percentage represents the percentage of payment records with a delay, not the percentage of loans with delayed repayments.
- Customer and account records may repeat across transaction and payment datasets because of one-to-many relationships.
- Financial totals must be checked for duplicate counting caused by incorrect relationships or filter context.
- Business findings describe the available dataset and should not automatically be treated as the performance of a real banking institution.

